{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending","id":1150480,"title":"Subjective World ending?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-17T15:08:55-07:00","id":1150480,"title":"Subjective World ending?","content":"What happens when the apocalypse happens? Like not all of them simultaneously, just one. Many religions have some great monster that will devour the gods and the earth if set free. Say the players set one such monster free and it wins what happens next? Does it need to chew through the other 9+ pantheons before it can fulfill it's prophecy of doom? Or does it simply devour the facet of the world that pantheon had with the others being untouched? I'm a little unclear as to how much the other pantheons myths are literally true when applied to the World<br /> <br /> I remember in 1e that the only apocalyptic plot (ragnarok) was isolated to being norse only and treated the other pantheons as non-canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T16:15:35-07:00","id":1150493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending#post1150480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when the apocalypse happens? Like not all of them simultaneously, just one. Many religions have some great monster that will devour the gods and the earth if set free. Say the players set one such monster free and it wins what happens next? Does it need to chew through the other 9+ pantheons before it can fulfill it's prophecy of doom? Or does it simply devour the facet of the world that pantheon had with the others being untouched? I'm a little unclear as to how much the other pantheons myths are literally true when applied to the World<br /> <br /> I remember in 1e that the only apocalyptic plot (ragnarok) was isolated to being norse only and treated the other pantheons as non-canon</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is one of the things that is very, very very much up to individual storytellers. There is no right or wrong way to handle this. (I, personally, think my own way to handle this is <i>really dumb</i>, needlessly complicated, but I've spent so much time making it work, and it prevents so many headaches that I can't ignore because I'm stupid about somethings and can't just ignore things.)<br /> <br /> I would say that no world-ending monster could kill off all the Pantheons though, things get too weird the moment you take a being out of their cosmology. I will normally keep Apocalypses centralized to individual Pantheons. Ragnarok for the Norse won't necessarily bother the Tuatha, even though they are in close proximity. The Son of Zeus situation will <i>probably</i> be an apocalypse for humanity, but it wouldn't cause problems for the Netjer. The end of the Fifth Sun for the Teotl will annoy them, but they'll just make a new one. The reason for this is not to let any one Pantheon become 'most important,' everyone is on equal grounds, all myths are true. The Norse End is just as true as the Teotl End is just as true as the Hindu End, but none of them are more true than each other, and none of them are more true than the Lack of Ends some cultures have. An Apocalypse is just as viable as not having an Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> But, how to handle this, there's only one world, and it gets messy with everyone squabbling over it. I tend to get really weird with it. You can say that Pantheons are limited to their region, that when Ragnarok happens, it will only destroy the parts of the world the Norse were influential in. But this gets messy quick since there is a massive amount of geographic overlap. I approach this with my own cosmology of Scion, that Midgard, The Land of Plentiful Reeds, Terra, Eriu, all of these are actually totally different places. When the Titans were imprisoned, Legend started fading from the world(s), and all of them got mush-mush-mushed together. The Earth is an amalgamation of all of these places, and the places most dependent on Legend to exist (Terra Incognita) or those far-far away from the 'Main Plot' of a Pantheon (Hyperboria) sort of 'Fade Out' as several hundred Earths all tried to fit into the same place. I use it to explain why Ireland is so much smaller than it apparently is in the Irish Myths, why the world doesn't have a rim of land beyond the ocean for the Greeks, all of those weird little issues of mythic Geography, things not being here that are totally supposed to be here, is because of the imprisonment of the Titans.<br /> <br /> And when you free the Titans... everywhere starts to come apart. Ireland stops being Ireland, and starts becoming Eriu. There are valleys, and forests that totally were not there last week. The island 'expands' or 'unfolds' as Legend comes back, Terra Incognita 'pop' back into existence. The world of the Tuatha has its own Rome, Greece, Egypt, and Persia, but it's not <i>our</i> Rome, Greece, Egypt, and Persia. It's how the Iron Age and Medieval Irish saw these places. For the Theoi, northern Europe sort of fades out the further you go and eventually you will hit Hyperborea. The world has a rim, and you can go touch the sky if you reach where it touches the ground. The 'Worlds' sort of slowly pop apart, each Pantheon's affairs their own. Unless, of course, the Scions, who are used to <i>their </i>Earth, want to fight for it, want to hold it together, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And when a world ends, that world does end. But it doesn't necessarily damage the rest of them. By the time Ragnarok has gone into full swing, Midgard would have 'popped' away from Earth. What would happen to, like, the coastline of Northern Europe? Or like all those people? I'd probably deal with it on a game-to-game basis.<br /> <br /> I find this helpful as it also helps avoid some clashing cosmologies. If Ragnarok kicked off, for example, why wouldn't the Tuatha roll up with all their weird, stupid powerful Relics and just go on a slaughter? It's their world, they don't want it broken. <i>Then</i> you're dealing with Fate-clashes. Lugh is armed with Fergarch again, and he stabs Surtr. Surtr can't die, he has a Fate for later in the story, but he just got stabbed with an armor-ignoring, always-fatal blade. That's a mess. If Apep is about to achieve victory and consume Ra, ending reality, you bet literally everyone will be rolling in from every Pantheon bringing all their goodies to just snuff out the issue in a half-hour. Even many Pantheon's Titans would show up for Apocalypses they didn't agree with, especially those that are 'end of reality' tier problems. Sure, the Tuatha and the Fomori are not always keen on each other, but you bet your last dollar that if they knew their fun fighting over Ireland was going to be spoiled because some big snake's about to eat some bird-headed guy far away, there would be armadas sailing as fast as you can blink of both peoples. Sure the Theoi and the Titans don't get on, but if Gaia was in danger because some twat on fire with a big sword was causing problems up north, family feuds could be set aside as Elder Cyclopses, Titans, Theoi, Gigantes, and Hundred Handed Ones storm northwards with irate fury that some barbarian is assailing their primeval mother. A whole lot of Titans don't want to see reality end, and in a situation where it was, &quot;End of World,&quot; that one Titan from that one Pantheon would not only have every other Pantheon rolling on in to smack the hell out of them, but would have an enormous about of Titans appearing, quite annoyed that someone is trying to break their world.<br /> <br /> This problem I solve with the separate worlds idea. The Tuatha don't really care if Midgard burns, not their problem. When the Deva are doing their cyclical reality thing, the Hittites are not concerned, it doesn't do anything to their lands even though it's restarting reality. When the Fifth Sun ends, and the Teotl are arguing over who gets to be the Sixth Sun, Sol is still riding away from Skoll. It helps keep everyone separated <i>unless</i> they are being thrust into the narrative by the activities of the players. The players can force Pantheons to interact in major ways, and the absence of PCs from some Pantheons in a Band lets me rationalize why those not-represented and not plot-relevent Pantheons are not coming to stomp on issues. It's not their world, they don't care, they have their own.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha don't give a shit if Midgard burns, but if one of The Dagda's daughters has a lover who is the daughter of Freyr, they could machinate having the Tuatha come crashing in, if they really wanted to have fun, bring the Fomori too. If Ra is about to die, and I have a Hittite Scion in the Band with the Son of Isis, the Thousand Gods of Hatti would come <i>ripping</i> across the desert of Duat, bulls the size of mountains hauling a massive chariot while Tarun shouts profanities and screams about how dare someone assail their eldest and closest friends. If I have a Band of two Netjer Scions, one Teotl, one Aesir, the players could totally rally the Pantheons to come get involved when Ra is about to be consumed, and Set has been somehow 'taken out.' If the Players don't go and drag Pantheons in, they're comfortable ignoring things since it's not their world. (or in the case of some Pantheons, they might not regard it as a real world)<br /> <br /> I don't honestly think this is the best solution however. This is just my solution, and it's <i>stupid</i> at the end of the day. It's a system designed for me to handwave away why I don't want to deal with the political ramifications of like, twenty different Pantheons all across the globe because someone raised a continent in the middle of the Atlantic. Or how I can have Apep be a legitimate, ever-present threat to the Netjer despite the fact that Ragnarok technically means that Apep couldn't eat Ra until the Ragnarok prophecy is far enough along that Skoll is swallowing Sol if their suns are the same. Or have to sit there going, &quot;Right, but what are the Trimurti going to do about this...&quot; in a game that has zero Deva Scions in it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T20:33:40-07:00","id":1150534,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think that's a really <i>brilliant</i> explanation for all of the &quot;real worlds&quot; and their apocalyptic myths - it explains all of the differences, gives everyone their own cosmology, justifies &quot;Odin/Geb/Tezcatlipoca made the world we live in [you are absolutely right, <i>for your world</i>], and gives great opportunity for somewhere to be destroyed [what <i>did </i>happen to Vanaheim, anyway?] without having to destroy all of Creation in the process. Imagine if Ragnarok happens, and the surviving Aesir are now refugees from their world, and wind up in someone else's; there's an entire campaign of possibilities there! I applaud this, and wish I'd thought of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T21:33:00-07:00","id":1150539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1150534#post1150534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think that's a really <i>brilliant</i> explanation for all of the &quot;real worlds&quot; and their apocalyptic myths - it explains all of the differences, gives everyone their own cosmology, justifies &quot;Odin/Geb/Tezcatlipoca made the world we live in [you are absolutely right, <i>for your world</i>], and gives great opportunity for somewhere to be destroyed [what <i>did </i>happen to Vanaheim, anyway?] without having to destroy all of Creation in the process. Imagine if Ragnarok happens, and the surviving Aesir are now refugees from their world, and wind up in someone else's; there's an entire campaign of possibilities there! I applaud this, and wish I'd thought of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am glad you like it! It helps me a lot deal with getting around having to explain every little thing to myself, which I find really helpful. It is also a really fun tool for making Terra Incognita flow more seamlessly into the world. After the Legend starts leaking back, if you go start digging in a Sidhe mound, you'll fall through someone's roof (and probably get yelled at a lot and probably forced to do something to make up for it) and there will legitimately be a large island off to the west that has a bunch of strange people on it who keep coming around and asking if anyone saw Oisin around somewhere, he was yay tall, noble of feature, bad at following directions.<br /> <br /> It also lets Hero start 'ramping up' in the area of legend and wonder. You don't need to go far-afield to find the magic any more. If the Band has messed up and broke some very Guardian-y things, such as removing the head of Bran the Blessed from where it protects England, there can just be magic <i>everywhere</i>. It seeps into the world like an infection. Suddenly there are Nymphs in pools, there are slumbering kings under mountains that were totally not there yesterday, and there are probably some irate Deities wondering who wasn't watching the children long enough for them to break something. It helps the masquerade problem, there never was one, but through the PCs fiddling with things, or gaining power, or generally breaking the status quo, suddenly there are Centaurs in Greece, and also a bunch of mountains that were not there? Also the <i>horizon isn't there any more</i> in Greece, and the sky looks slightly wrong now, like it's a physical object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T22:08:26-07:00","id":1150545,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine the apocalypse as being the divine equivalent to 'election day.' Or, rather, it's Fate's way of updating the pantheons when they become anachronistic to the rest of the World.<br /> <br /> During this process, the World is destroyed as most (if not all) of the current pantheon's members are cast down and in their place comes a new generation of deific figures who rebuild the World in their image.<br /> <br /> As the creators of this new World, they rule as higher beings until the next apocalypse, where the cycle repeats itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea is inspired by a combination of the fact that many doomsday mythologies ultimately result in the World being reborn after its perceived destruction, and creation myths dealing with the pantheons having overthrown their progenitors, who had previously done the same to their own forebears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-18-2017, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T22:17:21-07:00","id":1150546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1150545#post1150545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to imagine the apocalypse as being the divine equivalent to 'election day.'<br /> <br /> The World is destroyed as most (if not all) of the current pantheon's members are cast down and in their place comes a new generation of deific figures who rebuild the World in their image.<br /> <br /> As the creators of this new World, they rule as higher beings until the next apocalypse, where the cycle repeats itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea is inspired by a combination of the fact that many doomsday mythologies ultimately result in the World being reborn after its perceived destruction, and creation myths dealing with the pantheons having overthrown their progenitors, who had previously done the same to their own forebears.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a major apocalypse involving every pantheon that works out great (and would be awesome in a God campaign) but how would apophis or skoll eating the sun effect the World, would the sun go out? What about the other sun gods who are still doing fine? Would they also need to kill the other sun gods? or would that only effect the parts of the world their pantheons have dominion over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T22:51:18-07:00","id":1150547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1150546#post1150546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a major apocalypse involving every pantheon that works out great (and would be awesome in a God campaign) but how would apophis or skoll eating the sun effect the World, would the sun go out? What about the other sun gods who are still doing fine? Would they also need to kill the other sun gods? or would that only effect the parts of the world their pantheons have dominion over?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the sun gets swallowed, then the next generation simply creates a shiny, new replacement. As I said, many doomsday prophecies result in the world being reborn somehow. Which is difficult to imagine how that's possible if the sun is being digested in the belly of a dragon, or whatever.<br /> <br /> I'm currently imagining one of the endings to SMT: Apocalypse, in which your character defeats YHVH in order to usurp his position as creator of the universe. After doing so, you destroy the currently existing universe and replace it with one of your own design.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9O6jksMI0aI\" data-code=\"9O6jksMI0aI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9O6jksMI0aI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> As for how the multiple different apocalypses can exist within the same cosmology as each other. That's something I'm still having trouble figuring out. The simple answer would be to take the Ragnarok approach and just limit the game to a singular pantheon being canon.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I could make it so that every prophecy is happening simultaneously, and the ensuing chaos of so many conflicting Fatebonds ultimately rips the World apart, thus prompting Fate to 'reboot' the universe from the beginning. This time using a brand new cast of characters and with a (hopefully) better script than last time!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:29:49-07:00","id":1150975,"title":"","content":"@Watcher: well damn. Um, I hope you don't mind if I steal this for my own game, because that is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:18:29-07:00","id":1151015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1150975#post1150975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Watcher: well damn. Um, I hope you don't mind if I steal this for my own game, because that is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if people like it, people are more than free to use it! It's not purely my idea, I cobbled it together from the cosmologies of Aynie and Iry. Aynie has the idea of a 'sealed world' and Iry has the idea of the 'countless, merged worlds' which I wove together. I am glad it is serving of use to others!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T09:00:55-07:00","id":1151032,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>, I wish I could send my clapping sound to you through here, but as I cant, I will leave it to your imagination.<br /> <br /> That is an awesome cosmology, and I plan to use as basis (maybe change a thing or two, of course) for my own cosmology. Not just for Scion actually, for years I have DM a game of Mutants and Masterminds (for those who dont know, is a RPG for Super-heroes) and I have to deal with a cosmology with multiple Pantheons, dimensions, after-lives, time-travels, the whole overly-complicated comic book super hero stuff, so I know that trying to make sense of it is a endless and ungrateful job, as most players doesnt even care of how the universe works, but what you showed here is a cosmology that is worth to have their own comic book build upon. Or Movie. Or Tv Series.<br /> <br /> As you said, there is no right nor wrong way about it, and there all ways will be incoherent in a way or another (after all, we are actually trying to make many conflicting ideas coexist) but yours shows a lot of though and care, and should be in the book as a suggestion for the players to use. With your permission, of course.<br /> <br /> And thanks for letting it be Open to everyone. Glad for that )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 10-19-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T15:28:49-07:00","id":1151132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151032#post1151032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you said, there is no right nor wrong way about it, and there all ways will be incoherent in a way or another (after all, we are actually trying to make many conflicting ideas coexist)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hence my suggestion that all apocalypse scenarios happen simultaneously, and the consequences of so many conflicting fate bonds happening at once results in destroying the World. Afterwards, the surviving powers-that-be pick up the pieces and try to start over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T20:19:51-07:00","id":1151197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151032#post1151032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>, I wish I could send my clapping sound to you through here, but as I cant, I will leave it to your imagination.<br /> <br /> That is an awesome cosmology, and I plan to use as basis (maybe change a thing or two, of course) for my own cosmology. Not just for Scion actually, for years I have DM a game of Mutants and Masterminds (for those who dont know, is a RPG for Super-heroes) and I have to deal with a cosmology with multiple Pantheons, dimensions, after-lives, time-travels, the whole overly-complicated comic book super hero stuff, so I know that trying to make sense of it is a endless and ungrateful job, as most players doesnt even care of how the universe works, but what you showed here is a cosmology that is worth to have their own comic book build upon. Or Movie. Or Tv Series.<br /> <br /> As you said, there is no right nor wrong way about it, and there all ways will be incoherent in a way or another (after all, we are actually trying to make many conflicting ideas coexist) but yours shows a lot of though and care, and should be in the book as a suggestion for the players to use. With your permission, of course.<br /> <br /> And thanks for letting it be Open to everyone. Glad for that )</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm so happy you like it as well! I am now slightly embarrassed that I wrote the idea in such a rambling, incoherent way. If some people find the cosmology concept useful for their own games, maybe I will spin it together in a more elegant way, with some of the details I didn't put down, and my rationalizations for the different parts of the method from a game-running outlook as well as a All Myths Are True outlook.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T11:02:30-07:00","id":1151394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151197#post1151197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I'm so happy you like it as well! I am now slightly embarrassed that I wrote the idea in such a rambling, incoherent way. If some people find the cosmology concept useful for their own games, maybe I will spin it together in a more elegant way, with some of the details I didn't put down, and my rationalizations for the different parts of the method from a game-running outlook as well as a All Myths Are True outlook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see this idea expanded upon, with your additional thoughts and ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> maybe with consideration for 2E where the Titans aren't an equal universal threat, so maybe some other origin story for the Worlds becoming the World might be needed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T11:48:43-07:00","id":1151409,"title":"","content":"Make this a third vote for more detail on the idea - I think it's a very worthy alternative cosmology, and definitely very playable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T12:55:24-07:00","id":1151431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151394#post1151394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see this idea expanded upon, with your additional thoughts and ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> maybe with consideration for 2E where the Titans aren't an equal universal threat, so maybe some other origin story for the Worlds becoming the World might be needed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually one of the details I didn't expand into, we have been running our games with the idea that not all Titans are antagonistic for years now, so I actually already have that as part of the system. I didn't delve into it since I know not everyone does that. Lots of non-literal, and sometimes unintentional 'Imprisonments' like Lir being imprisoned by his grief, something which the Tuatha <i>never</i> intended, and worked against, but couldn't stop. He has no chains, no gilded prison, but his sorrow has kept him imprisoned for thousands of years. And not all Titans even get imprisoned, I've got explanations for that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151409#post1151409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make this a third vote for more detail on the idea - I think it's a very worthy alternative cosmology, and definitely very playable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, three it is. I study the Irish, so that's a good enough number for me. I will start spinning things up tonight. Is there anything in specific people would like to know how I handle? At base, I'm going to write the basic premise up more clearly than I did first, add the details I didn't touch on initially. (Not all Titans are Evil, Imprisonment as an Abstract Notion, The End of the Mythic Era / The Withdrawal of [most] Pantheons [and why can/do some Pantheons not withdraw], Dealing with Real-Life Chronology Issues, and The Return of the Mythic Era are the big ones) If people want anything specific touched on, just let me know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T17:30:59-07:00","id":1151510,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Watcher, Start a new thread listing these ideas. They look good enough to need their own little space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T17:48:34-07:00","id":1151512,"title":"","content":"Specifically if you could like, do some clear examples of what you're going for with one or two different examples each? Not super in depth but 'here's two short sentences making this idea more concrete to a game'. Anchoring the homebrew world building with specifics always kind of helps me understand better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T18:10:44-07:00","id":1151519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151510#post1151510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Watcher, Start a new thread listing these ideas. They look good enough to need their own little space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely will, I am just currently writing up the details. I started off giving myself a solid explanation of the issues I'm trying to address, seven big issues that I sought to address through this cosmology. I don't know if people will want to read that, but that's the only section I have completed thus far. It's 2,500 words because I used examples, and explained the challenges that these seven problems that the cosmology of Scion presents a Storyteller. <br /> <br /> I don't know if people will really want to read that, it was more of an exercise for myself to make sure I explain my reasoning, and showing how it addresses these things I identified as things that challenged me when running Scion. I'll probably wait until I have something more interesting for people to read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151512#post1151512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically if you could like, do some clear examples of what you're going for with one or two different examples each? Not super in depth but 'here's two short sentences making this idea more concrete to a game'. Anchoring the homebrew world building with specifics always kind of helps me understand better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can do that Alpharius. So, like, do you mean justify why I have made certain choices like I mention to Shadryx above, justifying the changes by showing the challenges I am trying to approach, or like, &quot;Not All Titans Are Literally Imprisoned, Lir is Imprisoned by Grief, Hadi, Skoll, Sol, and M\u00e1ni are imprisoned by chasing / being chased endlessly, and Raijin and Fujin are imprisoned by being converted to Buddhism by Kannon, but it isn't really working awesomely.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am currently in the process of working through ten example imprisoned Titans, and I am then going to use them to explain how I have changed what Titans are, and then <i>why</i> I made that decision from both a mythology, and a storyteller ease standpoint. Is that the sort of thing you're looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T19:31:48-07:00","id":1151536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151519#post1151519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or like, &quot;Not All Titans Are Literally Imprisoned, Lir is Imprisoned by Grief, Hadi, Skoll, Sol, and M\u00e1ni are imprisoned by chasing / being chased endlessly, and Raijin and Fujin are imprisoned by being converted to Buddhism by Kannon, but it isn't really working awesomely.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this, I find a few examples serve as kind of a grounding for me. Though I really would like to hear your logic on choices too just as a curious GM if you feel a need to type a bunch more. Your posts are always a pleasure to read","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T20:28:52-07:00","id":1151546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1150480-subjective-world-ending?p=1151536#post1151536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically this, I find a few examples serve as kind of a grounding for me. Though I really would like to hear your logic on choices too just as a curious GM if you feel a need to type a bunch more. Your posts are always a pleasure to read</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely can do that! I finished my rough draft, it's... a <i>bit</i> long at 7.3k words, and I feel a bit too dry. Tomorrow I will take the ideas, trim them down, structure it a bit better, write it in less of a dry voice. Hopefully I will have it up in the next day or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T19:58:12-07:00","id":1151827,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, if anyone wants to read the full details of my Cosmology minus one or two of the really weird bits, it is all detailed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151822-all-myths-are-true-my-cosmology#post1151822\">here</a>. (I'm really sorry it's so long)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:02:27-07:00","id":1152428,"title":"","content":"The Ragnarok chronicle I started with a local group (but never got to finish... due to various obligations the group had as individuals) didn't treat the other Pantheons as non-cannon... but did isolate the world from them. Fimbulvetr had cut the World off from the Overworld realms of the other Pantheons (in part due to the machinations of the Keepers of the World)... leaving only Asgard still connected to the world... but the Scions and monsters from the other Pantheons that were in the World at the time of impact remained... and were trapped in the World.<br /> <br /> \u200bThese Scions and Titanspawn now acted as wild cards in the outcome of Ragnarok... individuals that the fate of the Aesir had no hold or control over. This made them both a threat and an asset to the plans of Surtr's plans... for if they sided with the Aesir... he might not be able to bring them down as prophesy suggested. Thus, between the main three adventures, my players would have had smaller adventures to locate and possibly recruit these errant Scions and the more... reasonable... Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course when I first suggested this take on these forums... many roasted my idea as completely ridiculous and trash... saying I couldn't include Scions from other Pantheons because the legends of Ragnarok never mention them... but that was the entire point. The legends don't mention them because they are outside the fate of the Aesir... and thus have the potential to change that fate more easily than any of the Aesir would. I felt that this was an interesting twist to have with the setting... that while the players remained the focus of the game (with them being Aesir Scions and all)... their fate might be determined by the actions of a Scion that Ragnarok never considered a player in the final battle because the Scion wasn't part of the Aesir Pantheon.<br /> <br /> \u200bMore than that however... I had planned for the Players that survived to form a new Pantheon with the surviving Scions from other Pantheons to protect the newborn World when it reconnects with the Overworld Realms of the other Pantheons... especially since they have no idea what has happened in those Realms since they were cut off. How many of the old Gods survived... and what of the Titans that laid siege to those Realms? Without the Scions, the World and the other Pantheons to offer help... did any of them survive? Do they even understand what happened? Do they blame the Aesir for any misfortune... and transfer that blame to the surviving players? Just how much has the World changed because of what happened... both during Ragnarok and because of what happened in the other Overworld Realms?<br /> <br /> \u200bIt really is a pitty that the game never really got past the first few adventures... it would have been fun seeing how events unfolded. Still... thanks to the stretch goals of Scion 2... I might be able to rework that idea into the new setting to some extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}